Here is the complete, step-by-step master guide to fully root your Tecno Spark 8 (KG6k) running Android 11 (Build: KG6k-H6218MNOP-R-GL-230912V614) using Ubuntu.
------------------------------
## Step 1: Back Up Your Phone
Unlocking the bootloader will factory reset your phone and erase every single file, app, and photo. Move everything important to your PC or cloud storage before continuing.
------------------------------
## Step 2: Prepare Your Ubuntu Linux Terminal
Open your Ubuntu terminal (Ctrl + Alt + T) and run these commands to set up the official Android tools and configure USB permissions.

   1. Install ADB and Fastboot:
   
   sudo apt update
   sudo apt install android-tools-adb android-tools-fastboot -y
   
   2. Configure USB Permissions:
   
   sudo nano /etc/udev/rules.d/51-android.rules
   
   3. Paste these lines inside the text editor that opens:
   
   SUBSYSTEM=="usb", ATTR{idVendor}=="0e8d", MODE="0666", GROUP="plugdev"
   SUBSYSTEM=="usb", ATTR{idVendor}=="18d1", MODE="0666", GROUP="plugdev"
   
   4. Press Ctrl + O, then Enter to save. Press Ctrl + X to exit.
   5. Reload the system configuration:
   
   sudo udevadm control --reload-rules
   sudo service udev restart
   
   
