## Step 3: Unlock Your Phone's Bootloader

   1. On your phone, go to Settings > My Phone.
   2. Tap Build Number 7 times consecutively until it says "You are now a developer!"
   3. Go back to Settings > System > Developer Options.
   4. Switch ON OEM Unlocking and USB Debugging.
   5. Plug your phone into your Ubuntu PC with a reliable USB cable.
   6. Check your terminal to see if the phone is recognized:
   
   adb devices
   
   (Look at your phone screen; a prompt will ask you to "Allow USB Debugging". Check "Always allow" and tap OK).
   7. Reboot the phone into Fastboot mode:
   
   adb reboot bootloader
   
   8. Once the phone screen changes to a black screen with small text (Fastboot mode), run the unlock command:
   
   sudo fastboot flashing unlock
   
   9. Look at your phone screen immediately. It will prompt you to press a volume key (usually Volume Up) to confirm the unlock. Press it.
   10. The phone will wipe itself and reboot back to the initial setup screen. Proceed through the setup wizard.
   11. Re-enable Developer Options and USB Debugging exactly like you did in sub-steps 1-4.

